<description>
Reflect every foreground pixel 180 degrees through the single grey pivot pixel.

Input structure
- A black background contains a small colored foreground mask.
- Exactly one grey pixel sits near the mask and acts as the pivot.

Rule
- For each non-background pixel at (r, c), place the same color at
  (2 * pivot_r - r, 2 * pivot_c - c).
- The grey pivot maps to itself, and all original foreground cells are otherwise cleared.

Key insight
- The grey pixel is the center of point symmetry; the output is the same colored mask after a half-turn about that pixel.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "non-background foreground mask with a single grey pivot pixel",
  "transform": "reflect every foreground pixel 180 degrees about the grey pivot, preserving colors and clearing the original positions"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 3-9 rows x 3-9 cols, black (0) background
  pivot:
    color: grey (5), exactly one pixel
    position: placed so both the mask and its 180-degree reflection fit in-grid
  mask:
    description: irregular foreground shape adjacent to pivot (Chebyshev dist 1)
    cell_count: 4-8 non-pivot foreground cells
    distinct_colors: 3-4 (from palette 1-4,6,8; never 5)
    connectivity: 8-connected as a single component (including pivot) [observed]
    placement: all non-pivot cells on one side of pivot column [observed]
  transform:
    rule: reflect every foreground pixel 180 degrees through the pivot; clear originals
    formula: (r,c) -> (2*pr-r, 2*pc-c) preserving color; pivot maps to itself
    constraint: original mask and reflected mask must not overlap (except pivot)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first (build reflected pair, return one half as input)
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size H x W in [3..9] x [3..9]
    2. Pick pivot position (pr, pc) with enough room for mask + reflection
    3. Grow an irregular 8-connected mask of 4-8 cells on one side of pivot,
       each cell Chebyshev-adjacent to an existing mask cell or the pivot;
       use 3-4 distinct non-5 colors
    4. Verify all reflected positions (2*pr-r, 2*pc-c) are in-bounds and
       do not collide with original mask cells (reject or retry if violated)
    5. Place mask + pivot on black grid as the input
```
